{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And the children of Israel went out with a high hand.</b> In the sense of יָדֵינוּ רָמָה (Deuteronomy 32:27) — they were emboldened to prevail over Pharaoh and his army, who were not numerous enough to match them. By this He indicated that they had no knowledge of warfare, for indeed it would have been fitting to fear those few trained warriors more than it was fitting to fear the entire multitude of Egypt marching after them thereafter."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:24.997215622Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}